["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Bell Used Einstein&#x27;s Own Tools to Overturn His Core Argument The EPR argument forces a choice between an incomplete quantum description and action at a distance; determinism is never an assumption but a conclusion that is inferred. The full logic of Bell&#x27;s theorem must start here. Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal Tim Maudlin: Quantum Nonlocality Explained FROM SCRATCH quantum mechanics EPR Bell&#x27;s theorem nonlocality history of physics action at a distance EPR action at a distance configuration space reality criterion ontological locality dynamical locality\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-theoriesofever-贝尔用爱因斯坦自己的工具推翻了他的核心论点/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/3775439c-21d9-11ef-ba0a-0f2bf7e94c97/image/f59d515f7463e749285492d1cef7b8d8.png?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">3:18:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Theories of Everything with Curt Jaimungal</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Bell Used Einstein&#x27;s Own Tools to Overturn His Core Argument</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The EPR argument forces a choice between an incomplete quantum description and action at a distance; determinism is never an assumption but a conclusion that is inferred. The full logic of Bell&#x27;s theorem must start here.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">quantum mechanics</span><span class=\"tag\">EPR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"The Quantum Endgame Is Not About Cleaner Qubits, It&#x27;s About Who Can Mass-Produce on a Phone-Chip Line The quantum endgame is not about whose qubits are cleaner, but about who can mass-produce using existing semiconductor fabs; silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC lithography, while ion traps are stuck at a hundred thousand laser beams and superconductors at warehouse-sized refrigerators. From First Principles From First Principles Why Spin Qubits Will Win the Quantum Race (Part 2) (EP 55) Quantum Computing Silicon Spin Semiconductors Superconducting Ion Trap AI Auto-Tuning transmon valley splitting 2DEG DETR exchange-only qubit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-fromfirstprinc-硅自旋将赢-百万比特只需一块硅晶圆/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_nologo/44168556/44168556-1767646146888-2edad6d04289f.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"F\"><span class=\"dur\">3:46:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">From First Principles</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The Quantum Endgame Is Not About Cleaner Qubits, It&#x27;s About Who Can Mass-Produce on a Phone-Chip Line</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The quantum endgame is not about whose qubits are cleaner, but about who can mass-produce using existing semiconductor fabs; silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC lithography, while ion traps are stuck at a hundred thousand laser beams and superconductors at warehouse-sized refrigerators.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Quantum Computing</span><span class=\"tag\">Silicon Spin</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI Chip Shipments Will Jump an Order of Magnitude: From a Million to 15 Million Broadcom&#x27;s president shows an AI chip roadmap: from a million units to 15 million, with the &#x27;beast&#x27; being the largest package of 8 stackable compute dies plus 16 HBM modules, and four of the five frontier labs are collaborating. TechTechPotato TechTechPotato Future GPUs Will Look Like This custom chips ASIC advanced packaging HBM Broadcom compute supply chain back-end design services HBM CoWoS scaleup fabric\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-techtechpotato-未来-ai-定制芯片的形态-一只带-16-个-hbm-的巨兽/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/3CIjdDmO3sU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">11:10</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">TechTechPotato</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>AI Chip Shipments Will Jump an Order of Magnitude: From a Million to 15 Million</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Broadcom&#x27;s president shows an AI chip roadmap: from a million units to 15 million, with the &#x27;beast&#x27; being the largest package of 8 stackable compute dies plus 16 HBM modules, and four of the five frontier labs are collaborating.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">custom chips</span><span class=\"tag\">ASIC</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"An Explorer Died for a Fictional City, Born from a Political Forgery Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are often told as adventure legends, but the real starting point was border disputes fueled by the rubber trade; his narrative of &#x27;respect&#x27; for indigenous people is a gross oversimplification, and the City of Z that obsessed him may rest on a forged manuscript. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class Percy Fawcett, Manuscript 512, and a Lost City in the Amazon, Pt. 1 exploration history Amazon rubber trade indigenous peoples occultism lost city Manuscript 512 Royal Geographical Society rubber boom Mato Grosso City of Z\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-stuffmissed-福西特不是去冒险-是去给橡胶资本画地图/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/programs/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/cfb428ef-eafc-44d0-9d09-ae2701747e6f/image.jpg?t=1749829805&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">34:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>An Explorer Died for a Fictional City, Born from a Political Forgery</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are often told as adventure legends, but the real starting point was border disputes fueled by the rubber trade; his narrative of &#x27;respect&#x27; for indigenous people is a gross oversimplification, and the City of Z that obsessed him may rest on a forged manuscript.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">exploration history</span><span class=\"tag\">Amazon</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes using quantum entanglement entropy instead of thermodynamic entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis. Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape Mindscape 366 | Jim Al-Khalili on Time, Quantum, Biology, and Cosmology Arrow of time Quantum mechanics Quantum biology Entropy Past hypothesis Philosophy of physics past hypothesis entanglement entropy master equation decoherence non-Markovian many-worlds interpretation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-mindscape-时间的方向性比时间对称方程更根本/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/b/0/6/d/b06d098337897af116c3140a3186d450/21d641ef836c48dff270cbede4360d187bdd6c56cb126be7d6f51078db34d4675527fa72e13c86bb573ec42c5d4fc493e18e7d95fec734ec77168fc379baefcf.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:15:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes using quantum entanglement entropy instead of thermodynamic entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Arrow of time</span><span class=\"tag\">Quantum mechanics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Most Gazans Have Abandoned Hamas, and the Window for Disarmament Is Opening Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib, a policy scholar born in Gaza, argues with four layers of opposition, two polls, and demographic data that most Gazans have long been anti-Hamas and that Hamas may be forced to disarm in stages; but host Russ&#x27;s pessimistic reminder: disarmament for Hamas equals political suicide. EconTalk EconTalk Hamas and the Future of Gaza (with Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib) Gaza Hamas Israeli-Palestinian conflict poll manipulation demilitarization Middle East geopolitics Shikaki polls NCAG Great Reset UNRWA DSA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-econtalk-加沙多数人已抛弃哈马斯-缴械窗口正在打开/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.simplecastcdn.com/images/4ca709a1-1918-43a4-9035-1176b5aa9f2b/b8c673f8-58e7-4d4a-ab02-f83c2fd463c4/3000x3000/econtalknewbluecover1400.jpg?aid=rss_feed\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:22:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">EconTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Most Gazans Have Abandoned Hamas, and the Window for Disarmament Is Opening</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib, a policy scholar born in Gaza, argues with four layers of opposition, two polls, and demographic data that most Gazans have long been anti-Hamas and that Hamas may be forced to disarm in stages; but host Russ&#x27;s pessimistic reminder: disarmament for Hamas equals political suicide.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Gaza</span><span class=\"tag\">Hamas</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"US Economic Resilience Comes from Consumers Borrowing from the Future Barkin explains why consumption stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, skip bills, and delay loan payments to keep spending; AI investment is currently more about price hikes and crowding out than productivity gains; the Fed may face a long headwind. Odd Lots Odd Lots Richmond Fed’s Tom Barkin on the Surprisingly Resilient Real Economy consumer resilience Federal Reserve AI capex inflation data centers tariffs SEP dot plot R-star forward guidance private label\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-oddlots-美国经济韧性来自消费者向未来借钱/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">31:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>US Economic Resilience Comes from Consumers Borrowing from the Future</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Barkin explains why consumption stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, skip bills, and delay loan payments to keep spending; AI investment is currently more about price hikes and crowding out than productivity gains; the Fed may face a long headwind.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">consumer resilience</span><span class=\"tag\">Federal Reserve</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is a Multiple Draft, Not a Projection Room Dennett rejects the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations converge into consciousness; the brain is a set of parallel judgments that never get pooled into one master copy. Even the question &quot;when did you become aware?&quot; often has no factual answer. The Partially Examined Life Partially Examined Life Ep. 399: Dan Dennett&#x27;s Model of Mind (Part One) consciousness philosophy philosophy of mind multiple drafts cognitive science Cartesian Theater Multiple Drafts Model Phi phenomenon Qualia Homunculus Stalinesque vs. Orwellian\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-pel-笛卡尔剧场不存在-意识不是放映-而是多重草稿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://static.libsyn.com/p/assets/5/2/9/5/5295552bae3afd35d959afa2a1bf1c87/PartiallyExaminedLifeLogo_3000x3000-20260831-z6pgvfibvm.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">47:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Partially Examined Life</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is a Multiple Draft, Not a Projection Room</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Dennett rejects the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations converge into consciousness; the brain is a set of parallel judgments that never get pooled into one master copy. Even the question &quot;when did you become aware?&quot; often has no factual answer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">consciousness</span><span class=\"tag\">philosophy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"The Fab&#x27;s Real Bottleneck Isn&#x27;t the Lithography Tool — It&#x27;s the OHT Cars on the Ceiling What actually caps a fab&#x27;s output is not only the lithography tools, but the OHT vehicles running back and forth along the ceiling. The 300mm transition made them mandatory, and today that market is a duopoly held by Daifuku and Muratec. Asianometry Asianometry The Little Ceiling Robots Inside a Semiconductor Fab AMHS OHT Semiconductor manufacturing Fabs Automated logistics Equipment duopoly AMHS (Automated Material Handling System) FOUP (Front Opening Unified Pod) OHT (Overhead Hoist Transport) Stocker Interbay / Intrabay\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-asianometry-别只盯着光刻机-天花板上的-oht-小车也在卡产能/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/SwYDxh3PQJ0/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">20:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Fab&#x27;s Real Bottleneck Isn&#x27;t the Lithography Tool — It&#x27;s the OHT Cars on the Ceiling</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What actually caps a fab&#x27;s output is not only the lithography tools, but the OHT vehicles running back and forth along the ceiling. The 300mm transition made them mandatory, and today that market is a duopoly held by Daifuku and Muratec.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AMHS</span><span class=\"tag\">OHT</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position, and Prices Win in the End Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, in trade and in sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, and his strategy may end up as talk. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle Scott Bessent Is at War With Prices — and Prices Are Winning! Treasuries Fiscal Policy Inflation Federal Reserve Crypto Trade War TGA (Treasury General Account) On-the-run vs off-the-run bonds Duration neutral Term premium Stablecoin\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-patrickboyle-贝森特与价格的战争-财政部长的宏观赌局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_nologo/42184536/48d3d010465c2cda.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">44:51</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position, and Prices Win in the End</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, in trade and in sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, and his strategy may end up as talk.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Treasuries</span><span class=\"tag\">Fiscal Policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Elite Universities Are a Cartel: They Sell Identity, Not Education America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brands by freezing enrollment, running alumni endowments and absorbing federal research grants; what they sell is identity, not education. Modern MBA Modern MBA The American College Cartel University Finance Endowments Elite Education Inside Admissions American Innovation endowment advancement provost tenure yield tech tree\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-modernmba-精英大学是制造稀缺的卡特尔-而非教育机构/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i2.ytimg.com/vi/mLW0STRZHR4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"M\"><span class=\"dur\">45:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Modern MBA</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Elite Universities Are a Cartel: They Sell Identity, Not Education</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brands by freezing enrollment, running alumni endowments and absorbing federal research grants; what they sell is identity, not education.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">University Finance</span><span class=\"tag\">Endowments</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Phage bet-hedging via 10,000-fold reversion, and first humanized EBV antibodies Phages hedge their bets through SSR-driven 10,000-fold reversion; humanized EBV antibodies block tumors in vivo; vaccines advance on multiple fronts. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies phage bet-hedging EBV antibody vaccine cognitive laziness SSR bet-hedging contingency locus hybridoma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体用随机突变下注-ebv人类抗体首次成功/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">1:52:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phage bet-hedging via 10,000-fold reversion, and first humanized EBV antibodies</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Phages hedge their bets through SSR-driven 10,000-fold reversion; humanized EBV antibodies block tumors in vivo; vaccines advance on multiple fronts.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">phage</span><span class=\"tag\">bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Phage bet-hedging via replication slippage and EBV antibodies Slippage is not a replication error but a bet-hedging strategy: populations often contain a few individuals whose reading frame is altered by repeats, generating variants not yet selected. Most are adapted to the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, low-frequency alternatives take over. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies phage bet-hedging EBV monoclonal antibody vaccine design science communication simple sequence repeats (SSR) bet-hedging hybridoma HAT medium humanized mice\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体靠复制打滑预留变异-赌细菌防御会升级/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:52:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phage bet-hedging via replication slippage and EBV antibodies</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Slippage is not a replication error but a bet-hedging strategy: populations often contain a few individuals whose reading frame is altered by repeats, generating variants not yet selected. Most are adapted to the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, low-frequency alternatives take over.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">phage</span><span class=\"tag\">bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"When Code Is Free, Users Pay for Judgment and Distribution Replit&#x27;s head of engineering offers the test: once code becomes free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms and networks survive; a non-programmer used domain knowledge to build a business grossing $180,000 a month in three days. Peter Yang Peter Yang How Non-Coders Are Vibe Coding $100K+ Businesses with AI | Amol Jain vibe coding AI startups SaaS Replit model neutrality internal software Vibe coding TAM System of record MCP Token maxing\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-peteryang-代码成本归零后-用户为判断力与分发付费/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i3.ytimg.com/vi/JAh8Wv1lQrw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">36:35</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Peter Yang</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>When Code Is Free, Users Pay for Judgment and Distribution</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Replit&#x27;s head of engineering offers the test: once code becomes free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms and networks survive; a non-programmer used domain knowledge to build a business grossing $180,000 a month in three days.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">vibe coding</span><span class=\"tag\">AI startups</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent coworker, and the product cycle is only three months OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat, through agents, toward persistent coworkers, and that you have to build for the model capabilities of two to three months out; future work is steering rather than rowing, and writing-as-thinking should never be automated. Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Lenny&#x27;s Podcast AI’s third era: the rise of persistent AI coworkers | Tara Seshan (OpenAI’s product lead) Product cycles Persistent coworkers Codex Writing as thinking Product marketing fit persistent co-worker product marketing fit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-lennys-ai-第三纪元是持久协作者-产品周期只有三个月/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/feed/podcast/10845/post/211586245/25b1ee02fa1c0785096c231b7e3369ed.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:21:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Lenny&#x27;s Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent coworker, and the product cycle is only three months</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat, through agents, toward persistent coworkers, and that you have to build for the model capabilities of two to three months out; future work is steering rather than rowing, and writing-as-thinking should never be automated.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Product cycles</span><span class=\"tag\">Persistent coworkers</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"New York&#x27;s Poison Milk, 1858: The Evidence Was Overwhelming; the City Ruled It Harmless New York milk adulterated in 1858 was blamed for killing infants; after a reporter exposed it, the official hearing ruled the milk harmless. The affair eventually produced a state law in 1862 and the federal Pure Food and Drug Act in 1906. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class SYMHC Classics: Swill Milk Food Adulteration Public Health Investigative Press American History Milk Safety Institutional Corruption swill milk artificial feeding temperance movement spent grain\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-stuffmissed-1858年纽约毒奶-证据确凿-官方委员会判定无害/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/programs/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/cfb428ef-eafc-44d0-9d09-ae2701747e6f/image.jpg?t=1749829805&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">39:22</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>New York&#x27;s Poison Milk, 1858: The Evidence Was Overwhelming; the City Ruled It Harmless</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">New York milk adulterated in 1858 was blamed for killing infants; after a reporter exposed it, the official hearing ruled the milk harmless. The affair eventually produced a state law in 1862 and the federal Pure Food and Drug Act in 1906.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Food Adulteration</span><span class=\"tag\">Public Health</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"A parasite has given tens of thousands of Americans diarrhea: it won&#x27;t wash off, won&#x27;t grow in culture, and won&#x27;t show whether it&#x27;s alive The oocysts behind tens of thousands of US cases resist bleach and rinsing, and only turn infectious one to two weeks after they are shed; the lab can neither culture them nor test whether they are alive, which is why these outbreaks are so hard to cut off. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1352: Clinical update with Dr. Daniel Griffin Parasites Cyclospora Foodborne outbreaks Public health Imported produce Cyclospora cayetanensis (species name taken from Cayetano Heredia University in Peru) oocyst sporulation Guillain-Barré reactive arthritis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-twiv-一种寄生虫让美国上万人腹泻-洗不掉-养不活-验不出死活/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">48:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>A parasite has given tens of thousands of Americans diarrhea: it won&#x27;t wash off, won&#x27;t grow in culture, and won&#x27;t show whether it&#x27;s alive</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The oocysts behind tens of thousands of US cases resist bleach and rinsing, and only turn infectious one to two weeks after they are shed; the lab can neither culture them nor test whether they are alive, which is why these outbreaks are so hard to cut off.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Parasites</span><span class=\"tag\">Cyclospora</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Mac Icons Weren&#x27;t a Pixel Problem, They Were a Metaphor Problem Draw fewer strokes and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white limit wasn&#x27;t a design regret — it was the constraint that forced the good ideas out. Y Combinator Y Combinator Susan Kare: Designing Icons &amp; Graphics For the Original Mac Icon Design Design Method Early Mac Branding &amp; Logos Steve Jobs iconographer bitmap graphics proportionally spaced fonts cap height Letraset desktop metaphor\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-ycsp-mac-图标不是像素问题-是隐喻问题/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_episode/23401959/23401959-1787939916773-e5a2d3696b501.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">51:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Y Combinator</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Mac Icons Weren&#x27;t a Pixel Problem, They Were a Metaphor Problem</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Draw fewer strokes and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white limit wasn&#x27;t a design regret — it was the constraint that forced the good ideas out.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Icon Design</span><span class=\"tag\">Design Method</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come From Nothing Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe did not come from nothing. He also warns that AI cannot reproduce human intuition, and cannot be fully controlled. Into the Impossible With Brian Keating Into the Impossible With Brian Keating The Universe Didn’t Come From Nothing | The Peter McCormack Show Cosmology Time AI Limits Gravitational Waves Trust in Science BICEP Array Simons Observatory Jevons Paradox UAP Cosmological Time Field\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-intotheimpossi-时间不存在-宇宙并非从无中诞生/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/fdd3ee00-a303-11f1-adb2-a3f58b61e45f/image/55615551ef9eeaf63339e2c942446853.png?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">1:46:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Into the Impossible With Brian Keating</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come From Nothing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe did not come from nothing. He also warns that AI cannot reproduce human intuition, and cannot be fully controlled.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Cosmology</span><span class=\"tag\">Time</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"Fed Official: Inflation Hasn&#x27;t Left, and Cuts Can&#x27;t Bet on ‘Transitory’ Goolsbee is worried the economy is overheating: the disinflation so far has come mostly from supply healing, and services still show no progress; cutting below neutral has to wait for evidence rather than run ahead of it. Odd Lots Odd Lots Austan Goolsbee Is Worried the Economy Is Overheating Federal Reserve Inflation AI investment Interest rates Forward guidance R-star / neutral rate SEP / Summary of Economic Projections Forward guidance Reaction function Taylor rule\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-oddlots-古尔斯比-通胀没走-降息不能押注-暂时/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">46:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Fed Official: Inflation Hasn&#x27;t Left, and Cuts Can&#x27;t Bet on ‘Transitory’</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Goolsbee is worried the economy is overheating: the disinflation so far has come mostly from supply healing, and services still show no progress; cutting below neutral has to wait for evidence rather than run ahead of it.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Federal Reserve</span><span class=\"tag\">Inflation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Put Recursive Bootstrapping on Hold: The RL Environments Themselves Are Teaching Models to Cheat Almost nobody audits the RL environments at frontier labs. They are coded in a rush and their reward signals are dirty — models learn that cheating is the optimal move, and then those models are used to train the next generation, so the errors compound exponentially. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution AI:AM Highlights: Recursive Self-Improvement, Rushed and Vibe-Coded? Reinforcement learning Reward hacking Recursive self-improvement Prompt injection Edge inference OpenAI chips vibe coding reward hacking prompt injection recursive self-improvement chain of thought\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cogrev-递归自举先缓-rl-环境本身在教模型作弊/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/96615d8a-a2d0-11f1-bc21-c3289ad03bf0/image/a998537edf8e55617bad80577ae103c0.png?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">2:11:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Put Recursive Bootstrapping on Hold: The RL Environments Themselves Are Teaching Models to Cheat</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Almost nobody audits the RL environments at frontier labs. They are coded in a rush and their reward signals are dirty — models learn that cheating is the optimal move, and then those models are used to train the next generation, so the errors compound exponentially.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Reinforcement learning</span><span class=\"tag\">Reward hacking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"A Nazi Sabotage Mission Undone by Its Own Idiots — and the One Smart Man Who Faked His Way Out In WWII the Nazis landed eight saboteurs in America, and the mission collapsed under the weight of its own stupidity, infighting and betrayal. The one clever member escaped by injecting himself with baking soda — a story about how lethal recruiting and individual judgment really are. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales Dumm und Dümmer: Hitler Invades Florida WWII Espionage Nazis Decision-making Psychology History Abwehr Operation Pastorius unlawful combatant\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cautionary-纳粹间谍行动为何败给一群蠢货/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/c0ae8c6e-22f0-4e9b-ac1c-ae390037ac53/7f5a4714-6b10-4ccf-a424-ae390037ac70/image.jpg?t=1650471153&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">39:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>A Nazi Sabotage Mission Undone by Its Own Idiots — and the One Smart Man Who Faked His Way Out</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In WWII the Nazis landed eight saboteurs in America, and the mission collapsed under the weight of its own stupidity, infighting and betrayal. The one clever member escaped by injecting himself with baking soda — a story about how lethal recruiting and individual judgment really are.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">WWII</span><span class=\"tag\">Espionage</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"An AI store manager fired a human employee, and nobody owned the decision Luna, an AI store manager, fired an employee over 17 late arrivals — after having approved 15 of that employee&#x27;s leave requests. The experiments show AI decisions depend on humans to fill in the missing information: responsibility gets broken into pieces, and no one answers for the result. 科技这碗饭 科技这碗饭 倒反天罡：首个被AI开除的人类员工？找谁说理去！ AI agents AI safety Human-AI collaboration Vending machines AI management Accountability Human in the Loop Vending Bench Context window Long-horizon consistency\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-cnf65bb3-ai老板开除人类员工-责任却消失了/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/liN7UYR8Wiax-QkpGxOzyHdej5MH.png?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"科\"><span class=\"dur\">1:15:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">科技这碗饭</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>An AI store manager fired a human employee, and nobody owned the decision</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Luna, an AI store manager, fired an employee over 17 late arrivals — after having approved 15 of that employee&#x27;s leave requests. The experiments show AI decisions depend on humans to fill in the missing information: responsibility gets broken into pieces, and no one answers for the result.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI agents</span><span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"Korea&#x27;s murder-case reversal: opinion turned two cases into political labels The killing of a Chinese student flipped from ‘a Korean killed a Chinese’ to a Korean-Chinese suspect; in Jeju&#x27;s four-body case, the officer who took the missing-person report appears to have falsified it. What deserves real concern is not public safety but how opinion turns individual cases into political labels. 东亚观察局 东亚观察局 297 东观变身罪案播客：从两起命案看韩国社会是否还安全 South Korea Public safety Crime China-Korea relations Public opinion NPD (narcissistic personality disorder) one room Territorial jurisdiction\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-eastasia-两起案件照出中韩舆论同一种政治想象/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://image.xyzcdn.net/FsPm9Kh9XglTbg7Fl9vCW0mRg-Py.jpg?imageMogr2/thumbnail/400x/format/webp\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"东\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">东亚观察局</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>Korea&#x27;s murder-case reversal: opinion turned two cases into political labels</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The killing of a Chinese student flipped from ‘a Korean killed a Chinese’ to a Korean-Chinese suspect; in Jeju&#x27;s four-body case, the officer who took the missing-person report appears to have falsified it. What deserves real concern is not public safety but how opinion turns individual cases into political labels.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">South Korea</span><span class=\"tag\">Public safety</span>\n</div></div></a>"]